{"id":170101285485673,"type":"album","name":"Desperado","artist":"Eagles","year":1972,"weight":28,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710601.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-3cd3587f-8eaf-427b-bd84-cb2f21bed994/mbid-3cd3587f-8eaf-427b-bd84-cb2f21bed994-6643485103.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":11,"country":"US","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"Xg4Jp0WBDjE","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/09WBxbis5Sixt01FVMs8UM","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_k3UBMdBe0k-PWX6y1VCLJZVJogoUaKEco","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/eagles/desperado"},"desc":"Desperado is the second album by the American rock band Eagles. It was recorded at Island Studios in London, United Kingdom and released in 1973. It's a concept album, based on the Dalton gang and the Old West. Although the title track is one of the Eagles' signature songs, it was never released as a single. The album did yield two singles, though: \"Tequila Sunrise\" and \"Outlaw Man\". This album was slated for Quadraphonic release and even given a Quadraphonic catalog number, but never released in the format. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":106115726467187,"name":"The Eagles","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/178be204025c8d38a72113564b647baf/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":90510611927654,"type":"genre","name":"Country Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":425,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":251671925246370,"type":"genre","name":"Soft Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":418,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":186201380116213,"type":"genre","name":"classic rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":268,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":133646791193319,"type":"genre","name":"Laurel Canyon Scene","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":177455037556203,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements